  "gaps": [
    "Ledger covers the standard (GuidedPath) BS in Health Care Administration, Health Information Management; the Accelerated Master's Pathway variant (36 core / 48 specialization credits plus 12 master's-level credits) and the FlexPath option (program points, p. 191) are separate programs and not included.",
    "The capture does not state any residency requirement or which courses must be completed at Capella, so no requirement is marked institutional-only.",
    "Total requires a minimum of 54 quarter credits from the 3000-level and above; the capture does not specify how electives or general education must be chosen to satisfy this.",
    "The general education course list on p. 148 was captured in a scrambled two-column layout, so individual credit values for general education courses cannot be reliably matched to course codes; general education is recorded as a single 45-quarter-credit block with a minimum of 4 quarter credits from each category (Communication, Humanities, Natural Science and Mathematics, Social Science).",
    "Honors Pathway students complete PHI-H2005 (3), COM-H4005 (6), and SOC-H3005 (6), at least 15 quarter credits applied toward the general education requirement; this optional pathway is not itemized separately in the ledger.",
    "Transfer credit limits and policies are not stated in the capture."
